# A worked example: a small Alzheimer's disease slice of a SageBrain graph.
#
# Two participants, three samples, three genes, two pathways, one drug and one
# trial, with real identifiers throughout. Validated on every run of
# tests/validate.py.
#
# It exercises 17 of the model's 19 connections. The two it leaves out are the
# point of the last section below: an example that cannot be written honestly is
# telling us something about the model.
#
# IDENTIFIERS
#
# Resolved against the source registry (genenames.org, OLS, Reactome,
# ClinicalTrials.gov) rather than recalled. Prefixes follow Biolink's prefix map,
# since the model reuses Biolink terms.
#
#   HGNC:613            gene            APOE, ENSG00000130203
#   HGNC:620            gene            APP, ENSG00000142192
#   HGNC:17761          gene            TREM2, ENSG00000095970
#   MONDO:0004975       disease         Alzheimer disease
#   UBERON:0000955      organ           brain
#   UBERON:0002421      organ subregion hippocampal formation
#   UBERON:0000956      tissue          cerebral cortex
#   HP:0002185          pathology       Neurofibrillary tangles
#   REACT:R-HSA-977225  pathway         Amyloid fiber formation
#   REACT:R-HSA-9664422 pathway         FCGR3A-mediated phagocytosis
#   CHEBI:755918        drug            lecanemab
#   NCT02094729         clinical trial  BAN2401 (lecanemab) phase 1 study
#
# Where no ontology has the term, it comes from the AD Knowledge Portal data model
# instead (see the fallback note further down). All three are Attribute rows in
# AD.model.csv, and Source is that row's own citation:
#
#   adkp:BRAAKStage3        disease stage  BRAAK Stage 3       
#   adkp:FrequentDefiniteC3 pathology      Frequent Definite C3
#
# Participants and samples are presumed minted under https://w3id.org/synapse/ad/.
#
# Not in example:
#   sagebrain:has_status    DiseaseStatus has no vocabulary. The AD model's nearest
#     terms -- "no cognitive impairment", "mild cognitive impairment", "dementia" --
#     are values of its `diagnosis` column, not a separate status axis. So either
#     DiseaseStatus is a diagnosis under another name, in which case it duplicates
#     has_diagnosis, or it is the symptomatic/pre-symptomatic axis.
#
#   sagebrain:belongs_to    Biodomain has no vocabulary either: no ontology, and no
#     column in the AD model.

@prefix sagebrain: <https://w3id.org/synapse/sagebrain#> .
@prefix biolink:   <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/> .
@prefix rdfs:      <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

@prefix HGNC:   <http://identifiers.org/hgnc/> .
@prefix MONDO:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_> .
@prefix UBERON: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_> .
@prefix HP:     <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_> .
@prefix CHEBI:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_> .
@prefix REACT:  <http://identifiers.org/reactome/> .
@prefix NCT:    <http://identifiers.org/clinicaltrials/> .

# AD Knowledge Portal data model terms. PROVISIONAL: the model is a CSV today and
# has no published term IRIs, so this namespace presumes the most likely
# setup.
@prefix adkp: <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adknowledgeportal/data-models/refs/heads/main/AD.model#> .

# Study-local particulars are minted beside the model rather than inside it: the
# model is <.../synapse/sagebrain>, the data it describes is <.../synapse/ad/>.
# Data outlives and precedes any one model of it, and these participants may well
# be described by something other than SageBrain, so they do not belong in its
# namespace.
@prefix individual: <https://w3id.org/synapse/ad/individual/> .
@prefix sample:     <https://w3id.org/synapse/ad/sample/> .

###  Participants  ##############################################
#
# One case, one control. Both are sagebrain:Individual by subclass, so
# shape:IndividualShape reaches them without any inferencing.

individual:01
    a sagebrain:Case ;
    rdfs:label "participant 01" ;
    sagebrain:has_sample sample:01 , sample:02 ;
    sagebrain:has_diagnosis MONDO:0004975 ;
    sagebrain:staged_at adkp:BRAAKStage3 .

individual:02
    a sagebrain:Control ;
    rdfs:label "participant 02" ;
    sagebrain:has_sample sample:03 .

###  Samples  ###################################################
#
# Note that no sample is shared between participants

sample:01
    a biolink:MaterialSample ;
    rdfs:label "participant 01 cerebral cortex" ;
    sagebrain:source_tissue UBERON:0000956 ;
    sagebrain:has_pathology adkp:FrequentDefiniteC3 ;
    sagebrain:de_associated_with REACT:R-HSA-977225 .

sample:02
    a biolink:MaterialSample ;
    rdfs:label "participant 01 cerebral cortex, second aliquot" ;
    sagebrain:source_tissue UBERON:0000956 ;
    sagebrain:has_pathology HP:0002185 .

sample:03
    a biolink:MaterialSample ;
    rdfs:label "participant 02 cerebral cortex" ;
    sagebrain:source_tissue UBERON:0000956 .

###  Anatomy  ###################################################

# Use / map to UBERON for anatomy, using portal-specific vocab only when not possible

UBERON:0000955
    a sagebrain:Organ ;
    rdfs:label "brain" ;
    sagebrain:has_subregion UBERON:0002421 ;
    sagebrain:contains_tissue UBERON:0000956 .

UBERON:0002421
    a sagebrain:OrganSubregion ;
    rdfs:label "hippocampal formation" ;
    sagebrain:contains_tissue UBERON:0000956 .

UBERON:0000956
    a sagebrain:Tissue ;
    rdfs:label "cerebral cortex" .

###  Clinical vocabulary  #######################################
#
# GROUNDING FALLBACK. Where the grounding ontology (HP) has the term, use it 
# Where it does not, the term is from / minted in the AD
# Knowledge Portal data model (https://github.com/adknowledgeportal/data-models)

# For example, Braak staging is the worked case: no ontology on OLS has a Braak term at all,
# but AD model does define `Braak` with "BRAAK Stage 1"-"6", so the
# stage node below is an adkp: term rather than an external ontology.
#
# The same fallback covers plaque burden, via `CERAD`. It does not cover disease
# status or biodomain, which is why neither appears in this file at all.

MONDO:0004975
    a biolink:Disease ;
    rdfs:label "Alzheimer disease" ;
    sagebrain:has_trial NCT:NCT02094729 .

adkp:BRAAKStage3
    a sagebrain:DiseaseStage ;
    rdfs:label "BRAAK Stage 3" ;
    sagebrain:relates_to MONDO:0004975 .

# Pathology draws from both HP and AD model, examples showing that AD is used for graded categories.
# Plaque burden is graded, and CERAD is a scale of graded categories. 
# Currently HP term does not do graded categories; HP:0100256 asserts senile plaques are present (indicator only). 
# Tangles are the qualitative case, so they stay HP.
adkp:FrequentDefiniteC3
    a sagebrain:Pathology ;
    rdfs:label "Frequent Definite C3" ;
    sagebrain:relates_to MONDO:0004975 .

HP:0002185
    a sagebrain:Pathology ;
    rdfs:label "Neurofibrillary tangles" ;
    sagebrain:relates_to MONDO:0004975 .

###  Genes and pathways  ########################################

HGNC:613
    a biolink:Gene ;
    rdfs:label "APOE" ;
    sagebrain:expressed_in sample:01 , sample:02 , sample:03 ;
    sagebrain:participates_in REACT:R-HSA-977225 .

HGNC:620
    a biolink:Gene ;
    rdfs:label "APP" ;
    sagebrain:expressed_in sample:01 ;
    sagebrain:participates_in REACT:R-HSA-977225 .

HGNC:17761
    a biolink:Gene ;
    rdfs:label "TREM2" ;
    sagebrain:expressed_in sample:01 , sample:03 ;
    sagebrain:participates_in REACT:R-HSA-9664422 .

REACT:R-HSA-977225
    a biolink:Pathway ;
    rdfs:label "Amyloid fiber formation" ;
    sagebrain:associated_with MONDO:0004975 ;
    sagebrain:related_pathway REACT:R-HSA-9664422 ;
    sagebrain:de_associated_with adkp:BRAAKStage3 .

REACT:R-HSA-9664422
    a biolink:Pathway ;
    rdfs:label "FCGR3A-mediated phagocytosis" ;
    sagebrain:de_associated_with adkp:BRAAKStage3 .

###  Translational  #############################################
#
# `targets` ranges over biolink:Gene, so a therapeutic antibody against the
# amyloid-beta peptide is recorded against APP, the gene whose product it
# derives from. Worth knowing that this is a modelling compromise rather than a
# fact about lecanemab: the drug binds a protein aggregate, not a gene.

CHEBI:755918
    a biolink:Drug ;
    rdfs:label "lecanemab" ;
    sagebrain:targets HGNC:620 ;
    sagebrain:used_to_treat MONDO:0004975 .

NCT:NCT02094729
    a biolink:ClinicalTrial ;
    rdfs:label "BAN2401 phase 1 study" ;
    sagebrain:tests CHEBI:755918 .
